campaign unattractive. US media reports indicate that Trump is considering strikes after the midterms.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is EU putting profits over human rights in Vietnam?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7574080108abcbaca99875e5767bd89e57d1e59ad015d7a3a33d71eacbab394d</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:14:54Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T14:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-eu-putting-profits-over-human-rights-in-vietnam/a-79732812--0a31793443b5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-eu-putting-profits-over-human-rights-in-vietnam/a-79732812?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU and Vietnam are deepening economic and diplomatic ties, but closer cooperation raises concerns about whether Brussels is doing enough to address Hanoi's human rights record, labor standards and trade imbalances.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine: Life near the front line in Sloviansk</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3a8c0e5ce2c7bc5716ac82316b148bd8a5c087e50d6b13414c33d929b05c1f3a</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T11:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-life-near-the-front-line-in-sloviansk/a-79722636--5ef08a6d884a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-life-near-the-front-line-in-sloviansk/a-79722636?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Russian continues to attack Sloviansk in eastern Ukraine, thousands of residents refuse to leave or struggle to find a way out. For many, poverty, family ties and beloved pets make evacuation painfully difficult.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bulgaria: Concerns about security in the Black Sea dominate presidential election campaign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5b9a0b9925062385a95496361a446f540157fe16df756d3648e8325e8daac85</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-22T08:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-concerns-about-security-in-the-black-sea-dominate-presidential-election-campaign/a-79729094--fc0e44625feb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bulgaria-concerns-about-security-in-the-black-sea-dominate-presidential-election-campaign/a-79729094?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bulgaria's presidential election campaign has been shaped by recent drone attacks on ships in the Black Sea and the government's reduced support for Ukraine, making foreign policy a key factor in the first round.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Trump, Putin and Xi at one table, without Ukraine. What Moscow wants from the proposal and why Beijing might agree.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ff95dd57e7eca15e023198386472dbf38ed62a0d35b4d0e3098677ce0b89641</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T19:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-putin-and-xi-at-one-table-without-ukraine-what-moscow-wants-from-the-proposal-and-why-beijing-/a-79726190--eeff17927fb3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-putin-and-xi-at-one-table-without-ukraine-what-moscow-wants-from-the-proposal-and-why-beijing-might-agree/a-79726190?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Moscow is pushing for a summit with Donald Trump and Xi Jinping to discuss ending the war in Ukraine, without Kyiv or the EU. What does Russia hope to gain, and why might China be willing to take part?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Raids at far-right group's offices at European Parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a897ede298e42bc56d958c6437ad7d83fab1f1f7a08aa69196b6441a04167ed8</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T16:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/raids-at-far-right-group-s-offices-at-european-parliament/a-79724631--002ed5188c2e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/raids-at-far-right-group-s-offices-at-european-parliament/a-79724631?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Authorities searched the Patriots for Europe's European Parliament offices in a long-running funding inquiry. The group says the charges pertain to its predecessor and there is "no legal continuity" between the two.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia arrests German man, calls him a Ukraine 'mercenary'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d12405a692f04852ef7a9e8e8ba5d19ba6b618615d7be9d3b96715b216172fb</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T14:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-arrests-german-man-calls-him-a-ukraine-mercenary/a-79723871--8b55608360c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-arrests-german-man-calls-him-a-ukraine-mercenary/a-79723871?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Russian FSB agents have arrested a German national and accused him of fighting as a mercenary for Ukraine's military. They claim he deserted over unpaid wages and say he was a sniper who once served in the Bundeswehr.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russia frees jailed American Stephen Hubbard during Witkoff talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9c7f2c9c2ffacd84fc99297db03ce94cf862da6ea725bbd9942babc29fd25238</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T13:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-frees-jailed-american-stephen-hubbard-during-witkoff-talks/a-79719452--b6488d619654.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-frees-jailed-american-stephen-hubbard-during-witkoff-talks/a-79719452?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">During talks between Vladimir Putin and Steve Witkoff, Putin announced that jailed American Stephen Hubbard had been released. The Kremlin also said Russia was "in principle" ready to resume trilateral talks next month.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Pakistan-Taliban conflict: How India could benefit from shifting regional dynamics</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b4f8649bd1cf57bcf0dbdbc3da6a25f742e4e0f5a72c9398330cb7eb369073e5</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T10:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pakistan-taliban-conflict-how-india-could-benefit-from-shifting-regional-dynamics/a-79721426--f7ab516276cd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pakistan-taliban-conflict-how-india-could-benefit-from-shifting-regional-dynamics/a-79721426?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Pakistan's influence in Afghanistan comes under strain, India is rebuilding ties with the Taliban in Kabul. Can New Delhi turn this diplomatic opening into lasting strategic gains?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Australian MP Helen Haines loses both legs after car attack as suspect appears in court</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e034d8a67f563946a15987597a96b060f8f693a4176e901366d4180219294810</id><updated>2026-10-22T20:13:41Z</updated><published>2026-10-21T08:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-helen-haines-loses-both-legs-after-car-attack-as-suspect-appears-in-court/a-79697660--bbf1d96427b0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australian-mp-helen-haines-loses-both-legs-after-car-attack-as-suspect-appears-in-court/a-79697660?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Doctors have amputated both of Helen Haines legs after the Australian lawmaker was hit in an apparent deliberate attack. The suspected driver involved in the attack has appeared in court.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
